---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import {
  MentionListEditor,
  MentionListFiles,
  MentionListPeople,
  MentionListSkills,
  MentionListStates,
} from "../../components/MentionListDemo";
---

<Docs
  title="Mention List"
  description="A suggestion panel for @ files and / skills that a message box drives."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Mention List</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    The panel that opens when you type <code>@</code> or <code>/</code> in a message.
    The text field keeps focus and moves through the options with the arrow keys.
    Options can sit in groups, and status rows say when a source is loading, empty,
    or failed.
  </p>
  <section class="prose-section" id="mention-list-files">
    <h2 class="section-title">Files with @</h2>
    <p>
      Type <kbd>@</kbd> in the message, or press <em>Add file</em>. With Google
      Drive connected, results sit in a <em>Files</em> group and a <em
        >Google Drive</em
      > group, and each source has its own status row. Without Drive the files are
      one flat list. Search, files, and Drive in this example are sample data.
    </p>
    <MentionListFiles client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Mention list usage"
      code={`import {
  MentionGroup,
  MentionList,
  MentionOption,
  MentionStatus,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/mention-list";

<Textarea
  aria-autocomplete="list"
  aria-controls={open ? listId : undefined}
  aria-activedescendant={open && options.length ? optionId(active) : undefined}
  onKeyDown={moveWithArrows}
/>

{open && (
  <MentionList
    id={listId}
    label="Files you can add"
    status={loading ? <MentionStatus tone="loading">Searching your files…</MentionStatus> : undefined}
    announcement={\`\${options.length} files you can add. Use Up and Down to choose, Enter to add, Escape to close.\`}
  >
    <MentionGroup label="Files">
      {files.map((file, index) => (
        <MentionOption
          key={file.id}
          id={optionId(index)}
          active={index === active}
          onSelect={() => add(file)}
          media={<FileTypeIcon name={file.name} mediaType={file.mediaType} />}
          title={file.name}
          description="48 KB"
        />
      ))}
    </MentionGroup>
  </MentionList>
)}`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>MentionList</code> takes the listbox <code>id</code> and a <code
        >label</code
      >. <code>status</code> holds one or more <code>MentionStatus</code> rows under
      the options. <code>announcement</code> is read aloud when it changes, because
      a textarea keeps its textbox role and cannot say that a list opened.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>MentionOption</code> needs an <code>id</code> for <code
        >aria-activedescendant</code
      >, <code>active</code>, <code>onSelect</code>, and a <code>title</code>. <code
        >media</code
      > (a 16px icon, file icon, brand glyph, or small avatar) and <code
        >description</code
      > are optional. Long titles end in an ellipsis and show in full on hover. The
      active option scrolls into view.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>MentionStatus</code> has three tones: <code>loading</code> adds a spinner,
      <code>empty</code> is muted text, and <code>error</code> is an alert in the
      danger color. Pass <code>action</code> for a small outline button such as <em
        >Retry</em
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="mention-list-skills">
    <h2 class="section-title">Skills with /</h2>
    <p>
      One flat list with a book icon and the skill version. Typing <code
        >/c</code
      > at the start also offers the <code>/compact</code> command. Picking a skill
      stages it above the message.
    </p>
    <MentionListSkills client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="mention-list-editor">
    <h2 class="section-title">Rich editor panel</h2>
    <p>
      The rich text editor shares one panel for files and skills. An error wins
      over loading, and loading wins over the empty text. An option can have no
      icon or no description.
    </p>
    <MentionListEditor client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="mention-list-states">
    <h2 class="section-title">States</h2>
    <p>
      Each source reports its own status, so rows can stack: results with a
      source still loading, or two failed sources where only one offers a retry.
    </p>
    <MentionListStates client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="mention-list-people">
    <h2 class="section-title">People</h2>
    <p>Grouped people and agents with avatars. Click a row to select it.</p>
    <MentionListPeople client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Focus stays in the text field. <kbd>↓</kbd> and <kbd>↑</kbd> move the active
      option and wrap across groups, <kbd>Enter</kbd> or <kbd>Tab</kbd> picks it,
      and <kbd>Escape</kbd> closes the panel. When a search failed, <kbd
        >Enter</kbd
      > retries. Options and the retry button ignore mouse focus, so the caret never
      leaves the message. Touch rows are 44px tall; mouse rows are 36px. The panel
      rises in over 120ms and row highlights fade over 120ms; reduced motion turns
      both off. In forced colors the active option gets an outline.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
